  "habitat": "Well-developed woodland, especially riverine and other tall trees near water, and also broad-leaved woodland and clearings.",
  "summary": "An intra-African migrant that breeds in southern Africa in the wet season. In the Transvaal it is mainly present from late October and has left by April, with occasional records into early May. Adults have cinnamon upperparts, a lilac to purple throat and breast, a broad yellow bill, and blue wings and tail, without streamers. The sexes look alike. Newman's Birds describes the immature as greenish blue below with black streaks. A general account calls the juvenile a drabber version with a pale breast. The chick is not described.",
  "sampleData": false,
